**Operator type**: Elementwise unary operation
**Math**: `y[i] = |x[i]|` for all elements
**Input**: tensor of any shape, any dtype (float32, float16, bfloat16)
**Output**: same shape and dtype as input

**Design decisions**:
- Single kernel, one thread per element (or vectorized tile)
- Use `tl.abs()` intrinsic for absolute value
- Handle arbitrary shapes via flattened indexing
- Support float32, float16, bfloat16 via dtype-agnostic tl.load/tl.store

